    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d198">

                <pb facs="0363" n="231" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv01/pg231"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">761.93/7–745: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 198 <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Harriman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the President and the Secretary of State
                    </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d198-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">priority</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-07-07">7 July 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>(Personal and top secret for the President and the Secretary of State from
                        Harriman.)</p>
                <p>I took the occasion of Soong[’]s lunch
                    with me informally today to inform him of the President[’]s and your desire to
                    be consulted before any arrangements were concluded based on the Yalta
                        Agreement.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d198-f2"/> He readily agreed. Reference
                    White House message Number 310 Navy Number 061511.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d198-f3"
                    /> I also informed Molotov this
                    afternoon. He asked whether you had in mind consultation at Berlin or before. I
                    explained that if an understanding were reached in the next few days I assumed
                    that you would wish to be informed at once. He said he would consult Stalin. …</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d198-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d198-f1-content">
                <p>Sent by the United States Naval Attaché, Moscow, via Navy channels. Sent to
                    Washington; relayed to Truman and
                        Byrnes, then at sea, by the White
                    House Map Room in telegram No. MR 57 of July
                    8.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d198-f2" n="2" xml:id="d198-f2-content">
                <p>i. e., the agreement regarding entry of the Soviet Union into the war against
                        Japan signed at Yalta on February 11,
                    1945, by Stalin, Roosevelt, and Churchill. For text, see Executive Agreement Series No. 498; 59
                        Stat. (2) 1823; <ref
                        target="frus1945Malta#pg_984">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, The Conferences at Malta and
                        Yalta, 1945, p. 984</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d198-f3" n="3" xml:id="d198-f3-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
